abstract: >-
  A cross-platform graphical application for quantifying time-locked
  electromyographic responses. It measures motor evoked potentials (MEPs),
  compound muscle action potentials (CMAPs), cortical silent periods, M-wave
  recruitment curves and paired-pulse protocols such as SICI and ICF, reporting
  peak-to-peak amplitude, onset latency and area under the curve. Features
  include configurable filtering, automated and reviewable outlier screening, an
  interactive per-trial data inspector, Mmax normalisation with robust plateau
  detection, compensation of evoked-potential magnitude for pre-stimulus spinal
  motoneurone excitability by quantile regression, and BIDS-compatible output.
keywords:
  - electromyography
  - transcranial magnetic stimulation
  - motor evoked potential
  - compound muscle action potential
  - cortical silent period
  - corticospinal excitability
  - neurophysiology
  - signal processing
